{"name":"Cornflower Blue","hex":"#6c91c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cornflower blue","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bright blue color, with a tint of purple."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a bright blue color, with a tint of purple"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cornflower_blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cornflower blue","blocks":[{"text":"Cornflower blue is a shade of medium-to-light blue containing relatively little green. This hue was one of the favorites of the Dutch painter Johannes Vermeer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/CentaureaCyanus-bloem-kl.jpg/330px-CentaureaCyanus-bloem-kl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornflower_blue"},{"title":"Centaurea cyanus","blocks":[{"text":"Centaurea cyanus, commonly known as cornflower or bachelor's button, is an annual flowering plant in the family Asteraceae native to Europe. In the past, it often grew as a weed in cornfields, hence its name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Centaurea_cyanus_flower_001.jpg/330px-Centaurea_cyanus_flower_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centaurea_cyanus"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"h